      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "\"The Happiest Place in Town\" is a single by Australian rock/pop group Do-Ré-Mi released by Virgin Records and is the title track from their second album\"The Happiest Place in Town\". The song was written by, drummer Dorland Bray, bass guitarist Helen Carter and guitarist Stephen Philip. While the B-side \"Take Me Anywhere\" was written by Bray, bass guitarist Helen Carter and Philip; it is their first single not co-written with lead vocalist Deborah Conway. Do-R´e-Mi's 1985 single \"Man Overboard\" had been a surprise top 5 hit, but \"Happiest Place in Town\", from their second album, which was produced by Martin Rushent, had less chart success.",
